  "intrinsicContract": [
    "The original Fibre_transf_app observes the actual root homd_int(GG) o FF -> homd_id(E), with the target-index family explicit; no raw Op_funcd(FF) is used.",
    "The y projection is the ordinary modification component in Homd_coeff_cat; v uses the existing strict-transfor inclusion; f evaluates the reversed P-index arrow in Functor(I,T(Cat_cart)).",
    "The arbitrary epsilon, FF/GG, extracted filler cell, all displayed-identity specializations and the following constant-section observations are retained."
  ],
  "productRepair": [
    "The existing Functor_cart_cat(X,A*B) product split and Obj(Hom_cart) -> StrictTransfor disagreed on product carriers. StrictTransfor now has the matching componentwise product rule.",
    "Two product projections of strict_transfor compute through the existing inclusion while retaining a neutral whole head for naturality. No generic eta expansion is installed.",
    "The product target is the runtime discriminator; all runtime source/functor slots are inferred. The classifier-former rule retains the parameters needed to form its two actual component types.",
    "Placement follows the ordinary Transf_cat product rule. Earlier placement failed subject reduction because the ordinary output product was not yet available.",
    "An explicit constructor-only pair beta passed the first consumer but introduced a whole strict-naturality overlap and did not preserve the whole head. It was not retained.",
    "No new primitive, unification rule, supplied comparison or operational equality-proof argument is introduced. The kernel adds three structural runtime clauses."
  ],
